id: operation.error_handling
category: operation
status: verified
date: 2026-08-24
content: Errors are direct experience — the most trustworthy data. Every failure should be examined, encoded, and used to prevent recurrence.
notes: |
  Trust score for failure data: 0.95 (highest)
  Every error should trigger: examine → encode → prevent
  ToolRouter error classification → retry with adjusted params → fallback
  Never ignore errors silently — they are the system's most valuable teacher
  Failure patterns should be aggregated and stored in ExperienceReplay
tags: [error-handling, failure, learning, trust, reliability]
